  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 217 AM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nA cold front passage late Monday will lead to low end chances \nfor showers and thunderstorms in the overnight, mainly across \nsouthern Nebraska. Tuesday will be the coolest day of the week \nas the cooler air mass behind the cold front will keep \ntemperatures in the upper 60s to low 70s. For Wednesday WAA \nacross western Nebraska will moderate temperatures back into the\nlow 80s, while the rest of the Sandhills into north central \nNebraska will remain in the upper 60s to 70s. Thursday into the \nfirst part of the weekend, temperatures will remain cooler near \nseasonable to slightly below seasonable with highs in the 70s \nand lows in the upper 40s to low 50s. \n\nAs far as precipitation chances through the week, there will a \nseries of weak disturbances that move through the region mid-week \nthrough the end of the week with daily chances for showers and \nthunderstorms, at this time coverage remains uncertain, but less \nlikely to see any widespread precipitation. At this time the better \nchances for more widespread precipitation will be south into \nnorthern KS near the frontal boundary. There is however a stronger \ntrof that will move through late Thursday into Friday and at this \ntime looks to be the best chance of scattered to widespread \nprecipitation chances.",
